@startuml
title SSD - UC-12 - Manage Saved Blocking Rules (FST-048)
autonumber
actor Learner
participant "FocusDesktop System" as System

Learner -> System : requestBlockingRules()
System --> Learner : blockingRules(items, initially empty)
Learner -> System : createBlockingRule(displayName, typedTarget, action, category, enabled)
System --> Learner : blockingRuleCreated(id, fields, createdAt, updatedAt)
Learner -> System : updateBlockingRule(ruleId, providedFields)
System --> Learner : blockingRuleUpdated(persisted fields)
Learner -> System : setRuleEnabled(ruleId, false)
System --> Learner : blockingRuleUpdated(enabled = false)
Learner -> System : deleteBlockingRule(ruleId)
System --> Learner : blockingRuleDeleted(ruleId)

note right of System
  Application target: declared OS + executable path or process name.
  Website target: normalized domain including subdomains.
  Edits are atomic; duplicates are rejected without data loss.
  One empty policy remains after the last rule is deleted.
  Saved/enabled configuration is not proof of active protection.
end note
@enduml
